./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:53:5. **The one-cusp quartic horn is a saturated two-curve problem whose residual Kummer class is inverse.** Integration `2531a89d...` saturates Orevkov--Chau and forces a companion `A1` self-identification. Successor `bcc5148...` kills the independent-Kummer shortcut: `[E]=-[Phi]`, the collision is a monogenic index locus `u^mu-v^mu=0`, and Formanek makes the ruling coordinate primitive in the quartic field. No second ruling, no ramification of `pi`, and no `mu^2 | d1` follow.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:55:6. **The zero-cusp row is a connected etale `C3` torsor on the discriminant double plane.** Integration `f5dbad98...` promotes that gate and excludes the nodal control by `H1_et=0`. Boundary Fox coloring is insufficient. The prompt's constant-unit lemma, if later charged, would cut Kummer to anti-invariant `Pic(D)[3]`; until it is charged, both the unit summand and `Pic[3]` remain live.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:117:2. Close the two surviving rank-four arithmetic horns without duplicating a broader theorem: index-at-infinity or companion resultant for the one-cusp function pair; global `Pic[3]^-` for the zero-cusp double plane.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:128:Stale rankings: Avenue 2 as “the” principal proof backbone; cubic D3 as a live exclusion engine; raw class-group rank as an elimination gate (already retired); independent second Kummer class on the one-cusp horn; Fox coloring of the trefoil as a double-plane killer; any claim that closing rank-four proper blocks proves JC2.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:210:  A restriction (or residue) map from this group to `Hom(H1(Sigma_2), C3)` sends the forced etale class, in the zero-cusp row, to a 3-coloring of `K_infty`. Vanishing of the target does kill the torsor; nonvanishing does not create one. If the uncharged constant-unit lemma is later promoted, the kernel of restriction is precisely anti-invariant `Pic(D)[3]`, which is the remaining global gate. Localization, not coloring, is the content.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:214:1. **Non-simple inertia.** A generic `(3,1)` meridian is a 3-cycle, hence even. The sign homomorphism then fails to send every meridian to `-1`, the identification of `D` with the transposition support fails (already recorded in `f5dbad98...`), and (3.1) need not hold. This is the one-cusp row. Do not import (3.2) there.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:232:### 4.1 Cycle zero (no cusp): higher-genus knot at infinity
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:242:### 4.2 Cycle one (one cusp): monogenic index at infinity, or companion resultants — not a second ruling
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:250:**Companion resultant.** The norm identity `P_t(a)=lambda b^k c_0^mu` in `O(V)` is exact but does not bound `k` or the target degree of the coefficients. Pairing it with `q_H=b o H` can force `I_t` to meet `B` at the cusp, which the census forbids, or can compute `N=#(T intersect Phi)` incompatibly with the Euler/orbit identity. This is a polynomial resultant in the cyclic coordinates `(x,S)`, desk-scale once a presentation of `P_t` is not required to be global — it may be enough to work in the completed local rings along `Phi` and then recast the finite scheme `E intersect Phi`.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:258:The zero-cusp row has a connected etale `C3` torsor on `D`. The nodal control shows that 3-colorability of a trefoil at infinity is compatible with `H1_et=0`. The `Gm`-normalized cubic `T^3+xT+xy+1` shows that Euler-zero double planes can carry the class when the branch is not one-place. Those two controls already separate boundary from global.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:294:**Hoped-for implication.** The coincidence divisor `I_t` contributes at least one Orevkov--Chau boundary unit. Saturation of `4mu-1 = 2mu r + 2mu - 1` then contradicts the one-cusp horn.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:308:**Hoped-for implication.** Either `N=#(T intersect Phi)` violates the orbit identity `sum(nu - #D_x)=N+3`, or `I_t` is forced through the cusp, contradicting `|T31|=1` with an ordinary collision, or `S(0,y)` is forced to a single root, contradicting the self-identification.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:320:**Type.** Active zero-cusp gate. Subsumes Fox coloring.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:330:**Score.** 8. Directly the remaining zero-cusp content; the first test is one exact surface, not a family.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:406:**Minimal implementation.** One replay module that exposes those controls as named mutations (`--mutate-allow-degree-three` already exists). A new topology report must call at least the mutations that match its hypotheses, or declare typed `OPEN` why a control is inapplicable (e.g. one-cusp reports must not be required to 3-color a trefoil as a killer). Ordinary/`-O`/`-OO` identity and a planted pass/fail pair are the regression.
