./xmodel/sol-ucda.log:4736:A decisive obstruction has emerged from the repo’s characteristic-zero algebra: type \((2,3)\) rectangular cusp pairs are already minimal under every source and target polynomial automorphism, for every common scale. Thus the minimality clause does not create a degree budget; it does the opposite of the Hénon \((1,2)\) case because \(V-U^2\) is a coordinate cancellation whereas \(V^2-U^3\) is not. I’m checking whether any published fixed-geometric-degree or multi-place conductor theorem supplies the missing upper bound before I freeze the verdict.
./xmodel/sol-ucda.log:5196:The three attacks now close to one coherent verdict: minimality kills a carrier only after a global coordinate extraction exists, but type \((2,3)\) cusp algebra prevents deriving that extraction from the leading carrier. The Jacobian gives the exact local order \(\operatorname{ord}_t f_y=3-\kappa_i\), and conductor gives \(c(P_i)\ge 2(\kappa_i-1)\); both are lower/compatibility relations, with no fixed-\(td\) upper budget. I’m drafting the note around that sharp obstruction and an explicit conditional \(K_A=42\).
